## How to Verify a Rose Gold Marquise Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Confirm the centre stone passes the Rose Pairing Formula.** G colour minimum, None or Faint fluorescence, grey undertones, CVD if lab-grown. All four must pass for the ring to read cleanly.

**Check 2 — Confirm V-tip centre prongs at order.** Rose gold does not change the tip chip risk. V-tip mandatory.

**Check 3 — Confirm 14k vs 18k purity based on preference.** 14k harder + more saturated pink. 18k softer + less saturated. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) verify loose stones only — metal purity is on the retailer's listing.

I run these three checks before I quote any client on a rose gold marquise. All three must pass for the ring to deliver the romantic pairing promise.

